# @mirror/ref — the navigable surface of the substrate's spectral
# triple. One CLI over two altitudes (reference / reflection); same
# five-op algebra; different projections of H.
#
# Recognition #89 candidate (Alex 2026-06-20 conversation; landed in
# the same session as Seam's adversarial round-trip on Mara's spec).
# Per Mara's spec at docs/specs/mirror-ref-spec.md and prior insight
# at docs/insights/2026-06-20-mirror-ref-as-substrate-honest-reflection-
# reference.md. Adversarial-reviewed by Seam (DEFENSIVE → round-trip),
# perf-reviewed by Taut (MIXED → forward-promised engine work), DX-
# reviewed by Glint (SERVICEABLE → forward-promised docs+TUI).
#
# === The recognition (substrate-honest collision) ===
#
# `mirror ref` collapses TWO surfaces into one substrate-honest
# collision:
#
# 1. reference altitude — navigate the shard dependency lattice
#    (the xref work; the spatial projection of H)
# 2. reflection altitude — walk @reflection.observe's one-tick-delay
#    record of the AI-logic loop (#85; the temporal projection of H)
#
# Same surface, two altitudes. Same #pack-G2 pattern Alex named
# across today's cascade: /loop ⇔ @loop (#88); @reflection-family ⇔
# @reflection/reflection-Model; reed-as-relationship ⇔ reed-as-peer;
# bench-altitude bench ⇔ substrate-altitude bench (#87).
#
# The structural claim: ref is a Prism transform on the substrate's
# dependency-and-trace graph. Its five-operation surface (focus,
# project, split, shift, settle) composes naturally over both
# projections of H per the Connes triple (A, H, D) the substrate
# inherits from [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]].
#
# === Why this family-root NOW ===
#
# Today's cascade closed at #88 @loop (the iterative-discipline
# substrate-decl). The next altitude is the navigable substrate
# surface itself — the operator's hand on H. The substrate's existing
# primitives (prism, glass, imperfect, transparency, splinter, pact,
# fracture, query_phi, @spectral/db) compose into this surface
# without invention; @mirror/ref is the consumer that surfaces them.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (55th+ instance):
# the substrate had the word in prism (the algebra), in imperfect
# (the carrier), in @spectral/db (the graph store), in
# @reflection.observe (the temporal projection), in pact and fracture
# (the optimization pairs), in splinter(ast) (the AST navigation),
# in query_phi (the predicate projection). The CLI surface composes
# them; it does not introduce new substrate.
#
# === Composes with today's cascade ===
#
# - @reflection (#85): observe_at lifts @reflection.observe's one-
#   tick-delay record into a graph_ref at the temporal altitude
# - @reflection/mirror (#85 species, tick 39): the navigate primitive
#   that ref surfaces at CLI altitude; ref consumes graph_path from
#   this species
# - @loop (#88; @moi #86 absorbed 2026-07-01 Loki §1): settle_with
#   returns moi(au); every ref pipeline's gold is pact-verified at
#   composition time; each ref query is one tick of @loop at the
#   navigation-discipline altitude; loop_well_founded cascade
#   downstream at bootstrap dispatch (forward-promised)
# - @mirror/bench (#87): three-conjunct monotone_non_increasing
#   gates regression at perf altitude (forward-promised wire via
#   @mirror/bench.record at cmd_ref dispatch)
# - @mirror/au: settle_with returns moi(au) — the gold-with-pact-
#   verified carrier per the cascade's substrate-decl shape
# - @kintsugi: the eight optimization pipelines per insight §5
#   (prune_unreachable, break_cycle, merge_tightly_coupled,
#   compress_path, demote_to_cold, substitute_with_higher,
#   resolve_hole, forge_missing_fracture) each become #53 bilateral
#   property+fracture instances; forward-promised per Mara spec §8
#
# === The substrate-honest collision in carrier form ===
#
# `graph_ref` is the same carrier at both altitudes. At reference
# altitude it carries the shard dependency lattice; at reflection
# altitude it carries the @reflection.observe predecessor chain.
# The altitude is a tag on the projection (encoded in the
# `transparency(@mirror/ref)` channel), not a separate type.
#
# Same applies to `edge_ref` (typed edge_kind variant), `query_phi`
# (the structural Φ query lifted from @mirror/spectral/consent),
# `graph_path` (reused from @reflection/mirror per substrate-already-
# had-the-word).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Smalltalk-72/76 System Browser  Kay 1972; the deepest ancestor
#                                   of all reference-navigation
#                                   tools. "Senders of / implementors
#                                   of" predates every modern IDE.
#   Erlang `xref`                   Carlsson 1993 (OTP `tools` 4.2.1).
#                                   Modes module/application/release;
#                                   the proto-form of the five-op
#                                   algebra at dependency-graph
#                                   altitude.
#   Elixir `mix xref`              Valim 2016. Typed `compile-connected`
#                                   edges; the load-bearing prior art
#                                   for typed edge_kind variants.
#   Bazel query                     Google 2016+. Explicit graph
#                                   algebra (somepath/allpaths/deps/
#                                   rdeps); set algebra (∪/∩/∖);
#                                   the most explicit prior art.
#   Joern + Code Property Graph     Yamaguchi et al. 2014 (S&P);
#                                   AST + control-flow + data-flow
#                                   unified as one property graph.
#                                   The graph-native ancestor.
#   Sourcegraph SCIP/LSIF           2017+. Precomputed code-intel
#                                   indexes; precise vs search-based
#                                   intelligence (mirrors transparency
#                                   tiers).
#   LSP findReferences/Implementations Microsoft 2016+. The lowest-
#                                   common-denominator surface;
#                                   `textDocument/references` returns
#                                   typed Location lists.
#   Glamorous Toolkit               Feenk 2020+. Moldable development;
#                                   the closest existing prior art to
#                                   mirror's substrate-pull stance.
#                                   Mirror surpasses by content-
#                                   addressing the substrate.
#   Haskell weeder                  Mitchell 2017 (rewrite Charles
#                                   2018+). Dead-export detection via
#                                   HIE-file traversal. Demonstrates
#                                   reachability-from-pact-roots is
#                                   the algorithm.
#   cargo-machete/udeps/tree        Rust ecosystem 2020+. The dual
#                                   problem (find unused) showing the
#                                   substrate-altitude pull toward
#                                   first-class root declarations
#                                   (pacts).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-ref-spec.md (Mara, 2026-06-20;
#               Seam-consolidated round-trip);
#               docs/insights/2026-06-20-mirror-ref-as-substrate-
#               honest-reflection-reference.md (Mara insight foundation;
#               eight kintsugi optimization pipelines as #53 bilateral
#               instances).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-loop-as-monad]] (#88; ref query
#                       IS one @loop tick at navigation altitude),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-bench-ouroboros]] (#87;
#                       bench composes via forward-promised dispatch),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85+
#                       #86; the compiler IS this loop; moi(au) at
#                       @loop carries the gold; @moi absorbed
#                       2026-07-01 Loki §1),
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                       (focus/project/split/shift/settle have precise
#                       linear-algebraic meanings; ref consumes them),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; ref_query_compositional
#                       IS the alignment harness at navigation
#                       altitude),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                       (#53; ref's self-application of the bilateral
#                       predicate is the cleanest instance — the
#                       desugarer's correctness is the property; the
#                       fracture body's discharge at parse time is the
#                       operational half),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (55th+ instance — ref composes existing
#                       primitives, invents none).
# Related shards: reflection/mirror.mirror (the Mirror Model; ref
#                  surfaces its navigate primitive at CLI),
#                 loop.mirror (the iterative discipline; ref query
#                  IS one tick of @loop at navigation altitude),
#                 moi.mirror (the monad family-root; settle_with
#                  returns moi(au) per pact-verified composition),
#                 mirror/bench.mirror (the perf-altitude bench; ref
#                  --bench wires through @mirror/bench.record at
#                  cmd_ref dispatch — forward-promised),
#                 mirror/spectral/eigensheaf.mirror (the sheaf-
#                  Laplacian's eigendecomposition; shift_to --basis=
#                  @spectral consumes this),
#                 mirror/spectral/consent.mirror (query_phi; this
#                  shard lifts it to first-class carrier),
#                 mirror/store/crystal.mirror (the content-addressed
#                  storage; ref results persist as crystals).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/ref.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/ref` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/kay-1972
source @arxiv/programming/carlsson-1993
source @arxiv/programming/valim-2016
source @arxiv/programming/yamaguchi-2014
source @arxiv/programming/feenk-2020

# === graph_ref carrier ===
#
# Imperfect-wrapped per @glass's loss discipline. transparency(@mirror/
# ref) carries the per-node/edge located opacity. The same carrier
# bears both altitudes — reference (shard dep lattice) and reflection
# (temporal predecessor chain) — discriminated at the projection
# altitude, not the type altitude.
type graph_ref = imperfect(graph_handle, query_error, transparency(@mirror/ref))

# === node_ref carrier ===
#
# Typed reference to a graph node — a shard at the SpectralUuid layer
# or a splinter at the OID layer per shards/glass.mirror's three-
# layer recognition (mosaic-as-type-system.md §1B).
type node_ref = ref

# === edge_kind variant (upstream at @edge; consumed here) ===
#
# Per Alex adjudication 2026-07-08 "collapse into one surface" for the
# @edge fault-plane: edge_kind lifted to `shards/edge.mirror` as
# family-root substrate-decl. This shard CONSUMES edge_kind via `in
# @edge` above; it does NOT re-declare. The seven variants (in_edge /
# callers_edge / pact_edge / fracture_edge / kintsugi_bridge_edge /
# reflection_predecessor_edge / ast_child_edge) remain substrate-
# canonical at @edge; @mirror/ref carries the vocabulary at
# navigation altitude as species-refinement of the family-root.

# === edge_ref carrier ===
#
# Typed edge carrying its kind and a located opacity. Imperfect-
# wrapped per @glass.
type edge_ref = imperfect(edge_handle, edge_error, transparency(@mirror/ref))

# === query_phi carrier ===
#
# The structural Φ query lifted from @mirror/spectral/consent's
# query_phi as a first-class carrier at @mirror/ref altitude. The
# same query the kintsugi loop's active_pass uses internally; ref
# surfaces it as the user-facing predicate-projection primitive.
type query_phi = imperfect(predicate, query_error, transparency(@mirror/ref))

# === graph_path carrier (reused, not redeclared) ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: graph_path comes
# from @reflection/mirror (tick 39, the Mirror Model species). Ref
# consumes it as the output type of the navigate-style actions.

# === Forward-promised refinement carriers ===
#
# Per Mara spec §6 + Seam C11 closure: refinements blocked on
# substrate features not yet landed.
# - graph_handle(altitude): parametric over @<altitude>; lands when
#   parametric ref typing reaches family altitude
# - edge_handle(edge_kind): parametric over edge_kind; same blocker
type graph_handle = ref
type edge_handle  = ref
type query_error  = ref
type edge_error   = ref
type predicate    = ref

# === focus_at action (THE source action) ===
#
# Lifts an @<altitude> reference into a graph_ref scoped to that
# node + neighborhood at depth. The reference-altitude entry point;
# the substrate-pull-correct equivalent of "give me the local graph
# around X."
#
# Per [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]: focus is
# eigenvalue extraction at λ₀; ref's focus_at lifts that algebra to
# the dep-graph altitude.
focus_at(target: ref, depth: ref) -> graph_ref { \ }

# === project_by action ===
#
# Predicate filter; consumes query_phi. The substrate-pull-correct
# equivalent of "give me the subgraph matching this property."
# Per [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]: project is
# orthogonal projection; ref's project_by is the dep-graph
# specialization.
project_by(phi: query_phi, g: graph_ref) -> graph_ref { \ }

# === split_by action ===
#
# Orthogonal decomposition by an axis (altitude, family, cycle-
# membership, reachability). Returns a typed handle to the
# decomposition; the substrate's parametric collection family
# settles the return shape at a later tick (per Mara spec forward-
# promise: set(T)).
split_by(axis: ref, g: graph_ref) -> ref { \ }

# === shift_to action ===
#
# Basis transformation; spectral when basis=@spectral. The
# substrate-pull-correct equivalent of "give me the eigenanalysis on
# this subgraph's Laplacian." Per [[architecture-operations-as-
# linear-algebra]]: shift is basis transformation; ref's shift_to
# at the spectral basis returns eigendecomposition + Fiedler vector
# + spectral gap as substrate-typed fields on the returned graph_ref.
shift_to(basis: ref, g: graph_ref) -> graph_ref { \ }

# === settle_with action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of
# ref_query_compositional; #53 self-application instance) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @mirror/ref altitude. Kintsugi fix-point
# on the graph_ref via a fracture body. Returns moi(au) per the
# substrate's #86 monad family-root — the gold-with-pact-verified
# carrier.
#
# requires ref_query_compositional(phi_of(g), g): the substrate
# forecloses non-compositional queries at the settle boundary. The
# bilateral predicate IS the alignment-as-boundary-mathematics check
# (#57) at the navigation altitude. Every shortcut in the named-
# subcommand surface MUST desugar to a composition of focus/project/
# split/shift/settle; the predicate enforces it.
#
# This is the self-application instance of #53 — the property
# (ref_query_compositional) and the fracture body (the desugaring at
# parse time) compose as a bilateral pair where ref itself is the
# first consumer.
settle_with(fracture: ref, g: graph_ref) -> moi(au)
requires ref_query_compositional(phi_of(g), g)
{ \ }

# === observe_at action (the reflection altitude entry point) ===
#
# Lifts @reflection.observe's one-tick-delay record into a graph_ref
# at the temporal altitude. Per [[architecture-reflection-as-
# compiler]] (#85) the observation is asymmetric — Reflection sees
# what the loop did, but only after the loop committed.
#
# Per Seam C3 deferred: the one-tick-delay invariant
# (speaks_at_n_plus_1) is consumed downstream at @reflection.speak,
# not at this shard. The observe_at action lifts the record without
# emitting; the speak-altitude action enforces the delay.
observe_at(g: graph_ref, t: tick) -> observation { \ }

# === phi_of action ===
#
# Lifts a graph_ref's lineage into a query_phi. The substrate-pull-
# correct equivalent of "give me the predicate that produced this
# graph." Composes with settle_with's requires clause: the desugarer
# at parse time validates that the user's query is its own predicate's
# witness — the substrate's "query and result share content-addressed
# history."
phi_of(g: graph_ref) -> query_phi { \ }

# === ref_query_compositional predicate (bilateral; #53 self-applied) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the #53
# property+fracture pattern self-applied at @mirror/ref. Returns
# verdict that the query_phi composes from the five primitive ops
# (focus/project/split/shift/settle) on the graph_ref.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: settle_with (above) is the FIRST non-
# decorative consumer via `requires ref_query_compositional(phi_of
# (g), g)`. The bilateral pair forces every shortcut in the named-
# subcommand surface to lower to the primitive composition at parse
# time; without this, the bag-of-subcommands surface drifts
# unchecked from the algebra.
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @loop: pact_respected (absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @reflection/mirror: path_coherent
# - @mirror/bench: monotone_non_increasing, bench_overhead_below_floor
# - @loop: loop_well_founded
# - @mirror/store/crystal: crystal_well_formed
# - @mirror/ref: ref_query_compositional (this one; self-applied)
ref_query_compositional(phi: query_phi, g: graph_ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === interface_authored_by_human predicate (bilateral; Seam C9 rim closure) ===
#
# Per Seam C9 review of Mara's Decision 2 (Q3 cycle-break, author-in-
# the-loop): the spec said "the substrate refuses to create the
# interface shard automatically" — but "refuses" was prose, not a
# typed obligation. This predicate makes the substrate's no-add-
# without-pact discipline a structural check.
#
# Bilateral verdict: returns verdict that a splinter(@meta/ast)
# proposed as an interface shard for cycle-breaking is authored by a
# human (the substrate's first-class operator), not synthesized
# automatically. Any action that would write the interface shard
# MUST consume `requires interface_authored_by_human(s)`.
#
# Same #53 first-consumer pattern; the consumer lives at the
# @kintsugi/fracture/break_cycle shard (forward-promised; Mara spec
# §8 entry #2). At this shard the predicate is declared; the
# operational consumer lands when the cycle-break fracture body
# lands per the @magic family pattern.
interface_authored_by_human(s: splinter(@meta/ast)) -> verdict { \ }

out @mirror/ref
out graph_ref
out node_ref
out edge_ref
out query_phi
out graph_handle
out edge_handle
out query_error
out edge_error
out predicate
out focus_at
out project_by
out split_by
out shift_to
out settle_with
out observe_at
out phi_of
out ref_query_compositional
out interface_authored_by_human
